    "text": "Early product critique closed for **development-preview scope**. Three consequential defects were fixed and replayed within this same critique:\n\n1. **Overlapping surfaces obscured Industry and campaign controls.** Original run `12-53-07`, frames 002–009. Corrected run `13-05-48`, frames 002–015, shows readable Industry and opaque campaign forms.\n2. **Scrolling hid films and overlapped the footer.** Corrected frames 004–010 reach the real final film/end row, inspect its six credits, open Arthur Vale and his exact current employer, then restore the same studio scroll position through Back.\n3. **Typing a campaign name moved the camera.** Corrected run `13-29-04`, frames 009–011, shows visible text entry and native Left without changing camera pose, selection, week or state digest. Paired Left HID events and clean finalization were independently checked.\n\nThe [main replay](</Users/bruce/The Movies - P12A Living Hollywood Unity/Evidence/P12A/early-2026-09-10T13-05-48-186Z>) also demonstrates Save As naming, New Game naming, explicit overwrite confirmation/cancellation, deliberate selection and loading the other named campaign. The [focused keyboard replay](</Users/bruce/The Movies - P12A Living Hollywood Unity/Evidence/P12A/early-2026-09-10T13-29-04-098Z>) closes the observed typing defect.\n\nAuthored chronology, settled-history labeling and truthful “no announced production” are visible. This does **not** establish live rival production, three-world isolation, quit/relaunch persistence, large-text behavior or Gate A/B completion. Home was refused before injection and remains untested. No Owner acceptance is implied.",
    "textSha256": "ad3017b3b2e54b9b84b30b6d2d474dafc3fb5e37ab767a63957023f90481f8a7",
